{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/212235-jaguar-warrior-stats","id":212235,"title":"Jaguar Warrior Stats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-29T02:08:57-07:00","id":212235,"title":"Jaguar Warrior Stats","content":"I'm making a RAW Scion and wanting to add jaguar warriors as followers. Am I missing it somewhere in the book where it lists their stats? I seem to find other followers and antagonist stats but not jaguar warriors, which is even listed as an example in the followers section of the Scion Hero book. Any help is appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Nothing is foolproof for a sufficiently talented fool.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/981-bigwhitt","name":"bigwhitt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T03:27:56-07:00","id":212286,"title":"","content":"Jaguar Warriors are not printed in any Scion material. You will have to invent your own stats for them. <br /> <br /> Personally, I have used them in the past and simply taken the Elite Soldier template, then added 1 dot of each Epic Physical and a dot of Epic Perception to that. I typically give them the ability to make Bite and Claw attacks as a Jaguar, and sometimes for higher level ones, the ability to transform into a jaguar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T09:28:46-07:00","id":212536,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind birthright followers, while they may be named after a prominent pantheon-specific group, aren't necessarily so. Amazons, for example, even though they bear the Greco-Roman name are usable by just about any pantheon whose culture has a warrior-woman tradition. So, it may not be a matter of creating a custom template but rather adapting an existing one that works for you and your storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}